7e86298f (3097 1792838053101 "guenchi" (("w5vbequy" . 14982)) (put ((kind . section) (title . "landing f323") (src . "search: a scan costs what the hits cost; context's relevant step asks with distinct tokens\n\nA search over a long query built the whole (field x token) matrix for every\nlive block before asking whether every token hit, and compared substrings\nby allocating one per position; `context --for` on a large block, whose\nrelevant step searches with the block's whole source as the query, took\nseven minutes on a store of 17,000 blocks. The hits, their scores, their\nsnippets, the derived-word provenances and the unreadable count are the\nsame for every query; only the work changes.\n\n- store.sc: `search-state` judges a block token by token and leaves it at\n  the first token no field takes; the six stored and derived fields are\n  read before the token loop, so the unreadable judgement is made on the\n  same reads as before, and the editor-keyword hook is consulted before\n  the loop as before (its row is one of the columns the exit looks at). A\n  block that is a hit has its complete matrix; a block that is not has its\n  partial one discarded. `token-tier` and `substring-at?` compare in place,\n  a character loop at each position, no substring allocated. New exports:\n  `distinct-query-text` (prepare, tokens-of, first occurrences, joined by\n  single spaces), `search-positions-judged-count` (the (block, token)\n  positions the token loop reached, cumulative like `prepared-hit-count`),\n  and `token-tier` and `substring-at?` themselves so a fixture can measure\n  them alone.\n- context.sc: `relevant` passes the distinct query text of the block's\n  source; the title query is unchanged.\n- test/launch.pl: the anchor-gone note appends the facts on its line,\n  \"(setpgid <ok|ERRNO-NAME>, getpgrp <n|undef>, reap <timeout|exit n|signal\n  n|failed ERRNO-NAME>)\", on both variants; a watcher-only option\n  `--fault-setpgid ERRNO-NAME` injects a setpgid failure for the fixture\n  that reads the note, an unknown name refused at option parsing (rc 126,\n  a note, before the fork); the option is never forwarded to the anchor or\n  the command, and the suite's runner never passes it.\n- Fixtures: test/cli3.sc (SL-1 the positions judged bound at 2 x B for a\n  query whose first token every block takes and whose second none does;\n  SL-3 a token repeated three times answers as once; SL-3b \"Parse parse\"\n  and \"parse\" answer the same over Parse, parse and PARSE in different\n  fields; SL-3c `parser` and `parsed` both must hit; SL-4 `substring-at?`\n  and `token-tier` on a 1,000,000-character text against an absent token\n  allocate under 64 bytes per character, read through sstats; SL-5\n  `distinct-query-text` on a CJK/ASCII seam, a fullwidth form, repeats and\n  mixed whitespace, idempotent, and the same hits and 13 and 8 positions\n  for the text and its distinct query over a store where a first-token\n  search finds both blocks), test/supply.sc (SL-2 the answer equal under\n  the reversed token order where a derived word takes a token; SL-3b),\n  test/context-targeting.sc (the relevant step on a block whose source\n  repeats a word judges at most what the distinct tokens allow),\n  test/launch-self.sc (--fault-setpgid EPERM: status 126, the note\n  carries EPERM and \"reap exit 0\"; the runner passes no such option),\n  test/rows-baseline.txt.\n\nReadings on the code store (source mode, 17,110 live blocks): the relevant\nstep's search over a 29,660-character source 1.4 s cold and 1.3 s warm\n(before: 423 s), 27,899 positions judged against 61,596,000 by computation\nbefore; `context --for` on that block 3.5 s cold, 3.1 s warm (before: 420\ns). `search` through the dispatcher stays near 3 s, half of it the store's\nown load, which the search verb pays on every call; that is a separate\nitem.\n") (parent . root) (ord . 467))))
